Option: qr-one-line
Name: QR signs: print the address once on the directions sign
Does: tools/make_qr.py leaves out the Spanish line under the English one when the two are the same, so the directions sign prints 4701 Hartis Road, Indian Trail, NC once instead of twice (a new helper es_line in tools/make_qr.py). The consistency test accepts a sign with no Spanish line when the list gives the same words in both languages. The change to print/qr-signs.html is in the patch (that one line); the codes do not change. Other signs keep both lines, and the Hindi, Chinese and Vietnamese sheets already print a same-as-English line once.
Answers: d65 C (one address line; with qr-stronger-codes it is d65 D, both)
Conflicts: none
Requires: none
Host: any
Order: 70
Profile: filled
After: nothing is needed (print/qr-signs.html is in the patch); after a later change to tools/qr_links.json or reviewUrl run python3 tools/make_qr.py. If a print/ hunk does not fit because a sign changed, apply with git apply --exclude='print/*' and run python3 tools/make_qr.py
Strings: none

